1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,320
Dear friends who have been with us, who stand in solidarity with the Congolese people and who, no matter what, have stood with us to say, I will fight together with you. I will amplify your voice.

2
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:34,660
I thank you so much and I salute you for your courage and also for your hope because for us it's only hope that keeps us in this fight because we know that where there is life, even if it's one life, there is hope.

3
00:00:34,660 --> 00:00:48,460
One of the biggest mistakes that we make is we so much focus on the resources that we possess and we forget about the human, the human aspect of it.

4
00:00:48,460 --> 00:01:01,760
The most important of Congo is the human. Please look at the humans of Congo. Look at the amount of women that are being used as a weapon of war.

5
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:14,040
Look at the little girl of nine-year-old who was sexually abused just to humiliate, to humiliate the family, to humiliate the society.

6
00:01:14,780 --> 00:01:27,380
Look at this little kid who's just sitting there and his father has just been unalive and just sitting there with his sibling and not knowing where to go.

7
00:01:27,380 --> 00:01:43,380
What is happening here, it is affecting the entire Africa. It's affecting humanity and as long as Congo remains in a situation which is, as long as Congo is not free, no one will be free in Africa.

